  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>In 1 - 2, find the equation of a line with given slope and \( y \)-intercept. Write the equation in slope-intercept form.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="8ef284c1-00ab-48a5-88e3-a507f9d890c1"><problem><para>
      <para>slope 3 and \( y \)-intercept \( ( 0,5) \)</para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(y=5x+3\)</para><para>\(y=3x+0\)</para><para>\(y=3x+5\)</para><para>\(y=0x+3\)</para></problem><solution><para>\(y=3x+5\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(y=3x+5\). </para>
      <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y-y_1&amp;=&amp;m(x-x_1)\\y-(5)&amp;=&amp;3(x-(0))\\y-5&amp;=&amp;3(x)\\y-5&amp;=&amp;3x\\y&amp;=&amp;3x+5\\&amp;&amp;\end{array}\)</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
</document>
